      "prompt": "Use case: six independent original transparent PNG sprites for a first-grade post booth math game, in exactly 3 columns x 2 rows of equal square cells. Each sprite centered within its own cell at no more than 64 percent cell width and height, fully transparent gaps, no shapes touch boundaries, no grid or shadow. Fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut-paper contours, pine green and warm cream, muted sage and apricot and persimmon orange. Very clean and readable at 36 pixels. No words, numerals, arrows, printed marks, or watermark.\nTOP LEFT: cheerful deep pine-green snake head only, from top-leaning three-quarter view facing exactly RIGHT, small apricot cheek patches, simple dark eye and one curved mouth, short neck ends on the left for a body connector. Keep rounded nonthreatening.\nTOP MIDDLE: single sage green oval rounded snake body segment with one warm cream belly stripe and no face or tail, shape centered.\nTOP RIGHT: matching tapered sage green snake tail segment, thick rounded end on the LEFT and gentle taper toward the RIGHT, one cream belly stripe, no face.\nBOTTOM LEFT: exactly one small cream square perforated postage ticket with a large persimmon-orange five-point star at the center, one bold flat shape and clean border; star ticket will be repeatedly counted by the lesson.\nBOTTOM MIDDLE: exactly one small cream square perforated postage ticket, same size as bottom left, with a large simple deep-teal circle in the middle; circle ticket will be repeatedly counted in its own group.\nBOTTOM RIGHT: one larger friendly completion sticker, a warm cream badge with a small green postal cart and apricot star, isolated no background, bold clear silhouette. No letters or decorative particle effects.\nThe output must have genuine alpha transparency. All six sprites are separate, generous transparent margin to crop."
